    {
      "id": "58a7b434-5da8-592d-8251-8b7a9b3d8eaf",
      "name": "About",
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Reconcile: the inbox catches up with Stripe's event log\nWebhooks get lost: the endpoint was down longer than Stripe retries (3 days), or someone disabled it.\nEvery night this lists the last 30 days of handled events from Stripe's Events API (its retention),\nand queues the ones the inbox never got, each with its object fetched fresh in the pinned API version.\nThe processor then treats them like any webhook. Anything queued is announced: it means webhooks are failing.\n\n**Run now:** `POST /webhook/stripe-xero/reconcile` with the ops token header, e.g. right after an outage.",
